# Reversible Arrhenius binding whose energy patterns or reactant context the
# load-time expansion cannot price (issue #109), on the exact path: both the
# binding rule and its reverse half run as themselves, and RuleMonkey counts
# dG at each firing, as BioNetGen's network counts it per reaction.  phi =
# 0.35, so a rule that took 1-phi for phi, or the reverse, shows.
#
# The bond is weak (G = 6, Ea0 = 8), so about a third of each pool binds by
# t = 60 and every energy below moves its columns several standard errors.
#
#   AB / ABcd    Cooperativity across the bond, A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,d!3).C(a!2).D(a!3)
#                worth Gx = -2: a match through the new bond needs context on
#                both sides, so the rate is not a product of the two sides'.
#   PQ / PQcd    The same, anti-cooperative: Gy = +1.5.
#   LR / LRR     Wildcard bonds only, L(r!+,r!+), Gw = -1: binding the second
#                R to L(r,r).
#   MN           The pair named twice, M(r!1,r!2).N(l!1).N(l!2), on M(r,r,r):
#                matches over the pattern's two automorphisms.
#   ST1 / ST0    A state in a pattern: S(b!1,s~1).T(a!1), Gs = -1.2.
#   UVfree       A site the pattern requires free: U(b!1,c).V(a!1), Gf = 0.8,
#   UVbound      on U with c free and c bound to C.
#   WX1 / WX0    A state in the rule's own reactant pattern,
#                W(b,s~1) + X(a) <-> W(b!1,s~1).X(a!1): W(s~0) never binds.
#   GH1 / GH0    Context on the far end only, G1(b!1).H1(a!1,s~1) worth
#                Gs = -1.2: the rule's second reactant carries the term.
#   IJ2 / IJ1    Cooperativity across the bond whose far side can match twice:
#                I1(b!1,c!2).J1(a!1,d!3).K1(a!2).K2(a!3), Gx = -2, on a J1
#                that declares two d, holding two K2 or one.
#   SP / SU      A pattern with context on both sides that RuleMonkey splits
#                by class, A2(b!1,c!2).C2(a!2).B2(a~P!1,d!3).D2(a!3) worth
#                Gxs = -6, on a B2 with one free site in each class
#                (a~P and a~U), unidirectional: each site binds at its own
#                rate, drawn by the rule for its class.
#   YZ1 / YZ0    A bond in the rule's own reactant pattern,
#                Y(b,c!+) + Z(a) <-> Y(b!1,c!+).Z(a!1): only a Y whose c is
#                bound binds.
#
# The references are an ensemble of BioNetGen's network SSA (ssa).
begin model
begin parameters
  Ea0 8
  phi 0.35
  G 6
  Gx -2
  Gy 1.5
  Gw -1
  Gs -1.2
  Gf 0.8
  Gxs -6
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,d)
  C(a)
  D(a)
  P(b,c)
  Q(a,d)
  E(a)
  F(a)
  L(r,r)
  R(l)
  M(r,r,r)
  N(l)
  S(b,s~0~1)
  T(a)
  U(b,c)
  V(a)
  W(b,s~0~1)
  X(a)
  Y(b,c)
  Z(a)
  K(a)
  G1(b)
  H1(a,s~0~1)
  I1(b,c)
  J1(a,d,d)
  K1(a)
  K2(a)
  A2(b,c)
  C2(a)
  B2(a~U~P,a~U~P,d)
  D2(a)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b,c!1).C(a!1) 150
  A(b,c) 150
  B(a,d!1).D(a!1) 150
  B(a,d) 150
  P(b,c!1).E(a!1) 150
  P(b,c) 150
  Q(a,d!1).F(a!1) 150
  Q(a,d) 150
  L(r,r) 150
  R(l) 300
  M(r,r,r) 100
  N(l) 300
  S(b,s~0) 150
  S(b,s~1) 150
  T(a) 300
  U(b,c!1).C(a!1) 150
  U(b,c) 150
  V(a) 300
  W(b,s~0) 150
  W(b,s~1) 150
  X(a) 300
  Y(b,c!1).K(a!1) 150
  Y(b,c) 150
  Z(a) 300
  G1(b) 300
  H1(a,s~1) 150
  H1(a,s~0) 150
  I1(b,c!1).K1(a!1) 150
  I1(b,c) 150
  J1(a,d!1,d!2).K2(a!1).K2(a!2) 100
  J1(a,d!1,d).K2(a!1) 100
  J1(a,d,d) 100
  A2(b,c!1).C2(a!1) 200
  B2(a~P,a~U,d!1).D2(a!1) 200
end seed species
begin energy patterns
  A(b!1).B(a!1) G
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,d!3).C(a!2).D(a!3) Gx
  P(b!1).Q(a!1) G
  P(b!1,c!2).Q(a!1,d!3).E(a!2).F(a!3) Gy
  L(r!1).R(l!1) G
  L(r!+,r!+) Gw
  M(r!1).N(l!1) G
  M(r!1,r!2).N(l!1).N(l!2) Gw
  S(b!1).T(a!1) G
  S(b!1,s~1).T(a!1) Gs
  U(b!1).V(a!1) G
  U(b!1,c).V(a!1) Gf
  W(b!1).X(a!1) G
  Y(b!1).Z(a!1) G
  G1(b!1).H1(a!1) G
  G1(b!1).H1(a!1,s~1) Gs
  I1(b!1).J1(a!1) G
  I1(b!1,c!2).J1(a!1,d!3).K1(a!2).K2(a!3) Gx
  A2(b!1).B2(a!1) G
  A2(b!1,c!2).C2(a!2).B2(a~P!1,d!3).D2(a!3) Gxs
end energy patterns
begin observables
  Molecules AB A(b!1).B(a!1)
  Molecules ABcd A(b!1,c!+).B(a!1,d!+)
  Molecules PQ P(b!1).Q(a!1)
  Molecules PQcd P(b!1,c!+).Q(a!1,d!+)
  Molecules LR L(r!1).R(l!1)
  Species LRR L(r!+,r!+)
  Molecules MN M(r!1).N(l!1)
  Molecules ST1 S(b!1,s~1).T(a!1)
  Molecules ST0 S(b!1,s~0).T(a!1)
  Molecules UVfree U(b!1,c).V(a!1)
  Molecules UVbound U(b!1,c!+).V(a!1)
  Molecules WX1 W(b!1,s~1).X(a!1)
  Molecules WX0 W(b!1,s~0).X(a!1)
  Molecules YZ1 Y(b!1,c!+).Z(a!1)
  Molecules YZ0 Y(b!1,c).Z(a!1)
  Molecules GH1 G1(b!1).H1(a!1,s~1)
  Molecules GH0 G1(b!1).H1(a!1,s~0)
  Molecules IJ2 I1(b!1,c!+).J1(a!1,d!+,d!+)
  Molecules IJ1 I1(b!1,c!+).J1(a!1,d!+,d)
  Molecules SP A2(b!1).B2(a~P!1)
  Molecules SU A2(b!1).B2(a~U!1)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  AB: A(b) + B(a) <-> A(b!1).B(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  PQ: P(b) + Q(a) <-> P(b!1).Q(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  LR: L(r) + R(l) <-> L(r!1).R(l!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  MN: M(r) + N(l) <-> M(r!1).N(l!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  ST: S(b) + T(a) <-> S(b!1).T(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  UV: U(b) + V(a) <-> U(b!1).V(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  WX: W(b,s~1) + X(a) <-> W(b!1,s~1).X(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  YZ: Y(b,c!+) + Z(a) <-> Y(b!1,c!+).Z(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  GH: G1(b) + H1(a) <-> G1(b!1).H1(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  IJ: I1(b) + J1(a) <-> I1(b!1).J1(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
  SPU: A2(b) + B2(a) -> A2(b!1).B2(a!1) Arrhenius(phi,Ea0)
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
